    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d12">

                <pb facs="0102" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg6"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Buchanan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 416.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I confirm on the overleaf copy of your
                    telegram of the 16th instant, and of my reply of the 17th, in regard to the
                    recognition of the Hawaiian schooner <hi rendition="#italic">Americana</hi> by
                    the consul of this Government at Buenos Ayres.</p>
                <p>As you no doubt understand, the United States minister at Honolulu ceased to
                    discharge his diplomatic functions on July 4,1898, but until Congress shall
                    enact the necessary legislation our consul-general there has been instructed to
                    perform his commercial duties as heretofore, and in like manner the consuls of
                    the Hawaiian Government continue to perform their commercial functions in the
                    United States, and of course in foreign countries, during the interval before
                    Congress shall otherwise provide.</p>
                <p>Appending for your information copy of a telegram from the Acting Secretary of
                    the Treasury of the 17th instant upon the subject,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>




                <xi:include href="d12-a1.xml" xpointer="d12-a1"/>
